      "message": "Sorry for suddenly jumping into this patch after merging, I am rebasing RT pressure related patches but found conflict with this patch.\n\nFrom the naming the upper sentence should be written as:\nmin_capped_util \u003d min(new_util, capacity_min_of(i))?\n\nSo \u0027min_capped_util\u0027 means the required utilization has been capped? And from previous discussion, we should adjust value of capacity_curr_of(cpu) to reflect thermal throtting and RT pressure and use it to check if can meet waken task requirement; If we review the meaning for \u0027min_capped_util\u0027, it mixes the value for cpu capacity capping and utilization requirement.",
